---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy and optional analytics · OpenCyber Academy" description="Read every OpenCyber Academy lesson without an account. Analytics is optional and loads only after your choice.">
  <section class="section shell" style="max-width:800px">
    <div class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</div><h1>Open study, with optional analytics.</h1>
    <p>Books, lessons, exercises, the public API and MCP can be used without registering or accepting analytics.</p>
    <h2>Optional page-view measurement</h2>
    <p>With your permission, the site loads Google Analytics 4 to count page views and understand which public lessons are used. The tag does not load before you choose “Allow analytics”. Page URLs sent from this site omit query parameters. Google may process browser and device information under its own policies.</p>
    <p>Your choice is kept in this browser's local storage. You can change it using “Analytics preferences” in the footer. A new opt-out stops later page views from this browser, though it does not erase data previously processed by Google.</p>
    <h2>Student progress and chapter tests</h2><p>Signing in for saved progress and timed tests uses a one-time email code sent by OpenCyber Academy through Cloudflare Email Sending. Individually provisioned student accounts can instead use a username and password. D1 stores a salted password hash, never the password itself. D1 also stores an email address or account identifier, hashed sign-in codes and session identifiers, lesson and exercise progress, private lesson analyses, test answers, scores and any course-completion certificate record. Codes expire after 10 minutes; sign-in sessions expire after seven days and can be ended from your account page. Reading books and lessons never requires sign-in.</p>
    <p>For signed-in students, D1 records lessons opened and explicit completion actions, reading time while a lesson tab is visible, analyses they choose to save, exercise submissions and timed test attempts. Activity records distinguish site actions from actions made through a student MCP connection. The account page shows each student's own overall and per-course statistics, including best chapter-test scores and saved analyses. Anonymous reading does not create a D1 learning record. The public MCP remains open; private student MCP tools require a student session or personal AI key and never expose another learner's records.</p>
    <p>You can create and revoke personal MCP keys from your account. D1 stores a key label, prefix, SHA-256 digest, creation and expiration dates, last use and use count, never the complete key. Keys permit your connected AI to read and update your own study records; they expire after 180 days or immediately when revoked. Keep a key in the AI client's private credential storage. Signing out of the browser does not revoke a separately issued key.</p>
    <p>A public certificate verification link confirms the course, language and issue date without publishing your email address. Test answer keys are public learning material, so these self-assessments are not proctored exams. Reading books and lessons never requires sign-in.</p>
    <p><a href="/">Return to OpenCyber Academy</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
